{
  "step_1": "The decision reason considers whether a lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). Lottery A has a sure outcome of -500 Euros (100% probability), while Lottery B has no sure outcome (two outcomes, each with 50% probability). Therefore, the reason can be applied: it would prefer Lottery B, as it is the one without a sure outcome.",
